{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"keen-gymnastic-lemming","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_main_truthful_tally.py:87-106` only asserts that stdout lacks `converged`, although successful applied work must print an applied/total tally. Empty output can currently pass.\n\n## Approach\n\nStrengthen the existing liveness assertion to require the exact nonempty applied/total success line and add an empty-output negative control. This changes only the oracle, not reconcile behavior.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_main_truthful_tally.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nExercise successful nonzero apply output, empty stdout, and an existing failure/non-success control.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A successful applied reconciliation must emit the exact expected nonempty applied/total tally line.\n- [ ] Empty stdout fails the truthful-tally test.\n- [ ] Existing non-success/failure output expectations remain covered.\n- [ ] The focused tally suite passes.","id":"c181-20a2-1976-4d5d","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":3,"tags":["janitor","reconciler","oracle","rp36"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Require positive truthful tally output on successful reconciliation"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788314121933492001,"uuid":"be9c36f3-313e-4dce-a381-12a8515008e6"}